        historical: None,
        hints: (
            does: "A crew chasing a ship it hasn't come to action with loses this much morale a day (48 is 2 an hour).",
            play: "Raise it and long chases sour crews quickly, toward desertion and mutiny. Lower it and crews chase for nothing without complaint.",
            history: "Pirate crews voted on their captain's decisions, and a captain who wasted their time on fruitless chases was soon voted out.",
