            does: "Water a damaged hull takes in each hour on top of seepage, in proportion to the timbers she's lost.",
            play: "Raise it and battered ships founder soon after a fight unless they make port; repairs are worth paying for. Lower it and a battered ship limps home safely.",
            history: "Shot holes near the waterline were plugged by the carpenter, but a badly holed ship often foundered hours or days after the fight.",
